## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CMK usage, Key Vault integration, identity access, policy enforcement, and rollback planning at beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Customer-managed keys (CMK) for storage at rest
- Azure Key Vault with managed identities
- Storage Account encryption properties and keyVaultProperties
- Azure Policy to require CMK on new storage accounts
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// ARM-like snippet illustrating CMK encryption on a storage account
{
  "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
  "name": "[storageAccountName]",
  "apiVersion": "2023-01-01",
  "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
  "properties": {
    "encryption": {
      "keySource": "Microsoft.KeyVault",
      "keyVaultProperties": {
        "keyName": "<cmk-name>",
        "keyVaultUri": "https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net/"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate CMK policy compliance in CI/CD? 
- How would you handle CMK rotation without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region data governance with fine-grained access control, dynamic masking, and comprehensive auditability using Azure Purview, Synapse RBAC, Conditional Access, and Privileged Identity Management.

## Key Concepts
- Data classification and lineage tracking with Azure Purview
- Fine-grained access control in Synapse and ADLS Gen2
- Dynamic data masking with query-time enforcement
- Privileged Identity Management and Conditional Access integration
- End-to-end rollout, rollback, and testing methodologies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo example: determine if masking is required for a query
function requiresMasking(userId, dataset, column) {
  // Check Purview classification and user permissions
  const classification = purview.getClassification(dataset, column);
  const userAccess = synapseRBAC.checkPermissions(userId, dataset);

  // Apply masking based on sensitivity and user role
  return classification.sensitivity === 'High' && 
         !userAccess.hasColumnLevelAccess;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess storage security, policy enforcement, and rollback capabilities in a practical scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access
- Private Endpoints and VNET integration
- Managed Identities RBAC
- Secrets in Key Vault instead of config

## Code Example
```json
{
  "mode": "Indexed",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "properties.publicNetworkAccess", "equals": "Enabled"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rollback after applying policy?
- How would you handle temporary public access needs during migrations?

